import Wikipedia.HopfProblem.SheafCupProductCofaceCommutativity

/-!
# Low-degree Alexander–Whitney cup products from genuine ring cofaces

The standard coface identities imply the square-zero alternating
differential, the cocycle product, and explicit primitives for products
with incoming coboundaries. The pairing descends to the actual
kernel/range quotient groups and is additive in both variables. Its
degree-one skew commutativity and naturality under actual coefficient
ring maps are proved by explicit cochain calculations.

No resolution comparison, sheaf-cohomology identification, or desired
cup-product property is assumed by this algebraic construction.
-/
